                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "picked this up while looking for [url=https://steamcommunity.com/id/dohi64/recommended/351330]drod rpg[/url]-likes. guide a guy to the exit in dungeon after dungeon. grab keys, cash, potions, items and scrolls and manage resources. fight static enemies and try not to die or exceed the [b]mandatory hard move limit, going over means game over[/b]. the better the star rating the more xp. leveling only unlocks stuff, no stats, but you need to be a certain level to access new areas. level 24 for the last one, 77 3-star levels of the 82 until that point (120 total, with 'to be continued' at the end). [b]not only is it unfinished, there's almost no room for error for unlocks, only one level available at a time, no level skip and no undo.[/b]\n\nand of course it's an [b]incredibly lazy mobile port[/b]. some tapping, only separate audio toggles and windowed mode is non-resizable at full screen resolution, completely useless. there's an in-game 'wiki' with basic info unlocked as you run into them, but no level numbers while playing, they only pop up at the start. level complete screen with retry and next level buttons. [b]no tooltips or hotkeys, have to click everything.[/b] arrows move, esc brings up the exit confirmation, that's it.\n\nyou can move further, slaying enemies on the way and drinking potions out of pocket (most of the time), but [b]he might take a path you don't want and without undo it can be fatal[/b]. another annoying thing is [b]he won't pick up items even if there's room, only the one you clicked[/b]. cobwebs grab the first item, so makes sense later, but a better solution could've been worked out. [b]items can be dropped and picked up again[/b], doesn't cost a move, but [b]secret walls look identical to regular ones, so it's fucking trial & error[/b]. you'd think bumping into everything with arrows would do but [b]nope, only clicking works[/b].\n\nsince they were too lazy to demobilize their trash, there's way too many pop-ups and gems can be used to buy extra moves on the game over screen. and once you get some, powerups are selectable before attempting a level to add more coins, keys, hp, or open a door or kill an enemy. [b]the ui is broken though, so while using what you have is possible, the button for buying more with gems simply doesn't work.[/b] they're just in case you get stuck, but a broken non-fluff feature is a broken non-fluff feature. the game's been out since 2016, bug reported in 2017, devs saw it but it's [b]still not fixed because they're too busy shitting out a new 12 labours of hercules game every few months[/b].\n\nanother idiotic 'design decision': [b]layouts are fixed but levels gets rotated or even flipped between restarts[/b], sometimes entities get moved around too. absolute dick move to mess with orientation in a puzzler not about that. they mostly got rid of portrait nonsense but only the middle of level select is draggable, no scrollbar or mouse wheel and the usual incredibly long level map instead of putting 20 or more on one screen. a pain to find non-3-star levels or treasuries later. the chest should be clickable, with an up arrow to go back.\n\nthe idea is fine but with all the shortcomings, missing functionality, bugs and annoyances it [b]cannot be recommended or enjoyed to its full extent[/b], not at full price (5 eur) or any other amount. there used to be a free web version, not sure if it's still a thing.",
